{"id":"word:hebrew:H5337","type":"word","title":"נָצַל","subtitle":"H5337 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to snatch away, whether in a good or a bad sense","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to נָצַל (H5337) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 213 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"נָצַל (nâtsal) means to snatch away, whether in a good or a bad sense First listed occurrence: 1Chr 11 14."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"נָצַל","transliteration":"nâtsal","pronunciation":"naw-tsal'","strong":"H5337","lemmaId":"hebrew:H5337","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["לְ/הַצִּ֥יל","מַצִּֽיל","הִצִּ֥ילוּ","הִצִּ֥יל","וַ/יַּצֵּ֥ל"],"morphs":[["HVhrmsa",17],["HVhv2ms/Sp1cs",13],["HR/Vhc",11],["HVhp3ms",9],["HVhi3mp",7],["HC/Vhq1cs",7],["HVhp3cp",7],["HVhi3ms",7],["HVhi3ms/Sp1cp",6],["HC/Vhw3ms",6]]},"definitions":{"short":"to snatch away, whether in a good or a bad sense","usage":"× at all, defend, deliver (self), escape, × without fail, part, pluck, preserve, recover, rescue, rid, save, spoil, strip, × surely, take (out).","full":"H5337. natsal [ נָצַל 212 verb not in Qal; Pi`el strip, plunder ; Niph`al deliver oneself, be delivered ; Hiph`il snatch away, deliver (Ecclus Hiph`il Participle מצלת delivering Ecclesiasticus 40:24b (Levi conjectures יציל Ecclesiasticus 40:24a)); Late Hebrew Hiph`il = Biblical Hebrew; Biblical Aramaic Haph`el id. ; Syriac pour out ; Arabic intransitive tincturam exuit emisitque barba, ex cuspide excidit sagitta, etc., Kam Frey; Ethiopic III. evulsum or abruptum excidere e suo loco , Di 698 ); — Niph`al Perfect 1plural נִצַּלְנוּ Jer 7:10 ; Imperfect יִנָּצֵל Deut 23:16 , + 1singular אִנָָּֽצְלָה Psa 69:15 , + 8 t. Imperfect; Infinitive הַנָּצֵל Isa 20:6 3 t. — 1 reflexive tear oneself away, deliver oneself: absolute Prov 6:3 ; Ezek 14:16 , 18 ; 2Kin 19:11 = Isa 37:11 ; with מִיַּד Prov 6:5 ; אֶל ֗֗֗ מֵעִ escape from-unto Deut 23:16 . 2 passive , be torn, out or away הָאֲרִי מִמִּי Amos 3:12 ; be delivered , absolute Gen 32:31 ; Jer 7:10 ; Psa 33:16 ; Micah 4:30 מִמְּנֵי Isa 20:6 ; מִכַּף Hab 2:9 ; מִן Psa 69:15 . Pi`el Perfect 2masculine plural נִצַּלְתֶּם Exod 3:22 ; Imperfect יְנַצֵּל Ezek 14:14 2 t.; — 1 strip of, spoil , absolute 2Chr 20:25 ; with accusative of person Exod 3:22 ; 12:36 (J). 2 deliver , with accusative נַפְשָׁם Ezek 14:14 . Hiph`il 190 Perfect הִצִּיל Exod 12:27 ; 2 masculine singular הִצַּ֫לְתָּ 5:23 50t. Perfect; Imperfect יַּצִּיל 2Kin 17:39 ; יַצֵּל Gen 31:9 63t. Imperfect; Imperative הַצֵּל Prov 24:11 ; הַצִּ֫ילָה Psa 22:21 ; suffix הַצִּילֵנִי Gen 32:12 24 t. Imperative; Infinitive absolute הַצֵּל 2Kin 18:30 4 t.; construct הַצִּיל Gen 37:22-23 t. Infinitive; Participle מַצִּיל Deut 32:39 16 t. Participle — 1 take away, snatch away , e.g. property Gen 31:9-10 , (E) Hosea 2:11 , prey from the mouth of animals 1Sam 17:35 ; Amos 3:12 ; Ezek 34:10 , words of ׳י from the mouth Psa 119:43 ; בֵּינֵיהֶם מַצִּיל וְאֵין 2Sam 14:6 and there was none to tear them apart (two fighting); וְהִצִּיל עֵינֵנוּ 20:6 and take away our eye (elude our sight, Ges; Ew We after ᵐ5 cast shadow over our eye, denominative from צֵל Bö Th after ᵑ6 tear away our eye, harm us irretrievably, see Dr 1826. 2 .; HPS escape from us [ מִמֶּנּוּ , as ᵐ5 L ], compare Bu [ וְנִצַּל ]). 2 rescue, recover, e.g. cities Judg 11:26 ; wives and property 1Sam 30:8 , 18 , 22 . 3 deliver from: a. enemies and troubles , absolute 1Sam 12:21 ; Prov 19:19 ; Isa 50:2 ; Jer 39:17 ; מַצִּיל אֵין Judg 18:28 ; Job 5:4 ; 10:7 ; Psa 7:3 ; 50:22 ; 71:11 ; Isa 5:29 ; 42:22 ; 43:13 ; Daniel 8:47; Hosea 5:14 ; Micah 5:7 ; with accusative Gen 18:8 (E), Exod 5:23 ; 12:27 (J), Deut 23:15 39t.; נַפְשׁוֺ הַצִּיל Isa 44:20 ; 47:14 ; Ezek 3:19 , 21 ; 14:20 ; 33:19 ; with מִן from Micah 5:6 25t.; מִיַּד from the hand or power of Gen 32:12 ; Exod 2:19 (J) + 57 t.; יַד מִתַּחַת 18:10 (E); מִכַּף 2Sam 14:16 ; 19:10 ; 22:1 = Psa 18:1 , 2Kin 20:6 = Isa 38:6 ; 2Chr 32:11 ; Ezra 8:31 . b. from death Prov 11:16 ; 12:6 ; מִמּוֺת Josh 2:13 (J), Psa 33:19 ; Psalm 56:14; Prov 10:12 = 11:4 ; מִשְּׁאוֺל Psa 86:13 ; Prov 23:14 . 4 deliver from sin and guilt (in late writings), מִכָּלמְּֿשָׁעַי Psa 39:9 from all my trangression ; מִדָּמִים 51:6 from bloodguiltiness ; עַלחַֿטּאֹתֵינוּ וְכַמֵּר הַצִּילֵנוּ 79:9 deliver us and cover over all our sins ; probably also הַצִּילֵנִי כְּאִמְרָֽתְךָ 119:170 . Hoph`al Participle מֻצּל ; — מִשְּׂרֵטָה מֻצָּל כְּאוּד Amos 4:11 as a brand plucked out of the burning ; מֵאֵשׁ Zech 3:2 from the fire. Hithpa`el אֶתעֶֿדְיָם וַיִּתְנַצְּלוּ Exod 33:6 (E) and they stripped themselves of their ornaments. [ נְצַל ] verb Haph`el rescue, deliver (see Biblical Hebrew, Egyptian Aramaic הנצל take away , S-C C 10, D 18 ); — of God, absolute: Participle active מַצִּל Dan 6:28 , Infinitive לְהַצָּלָה 3:29 ; of man, suffix person לְהַצָּלוּתֵהּ 6:15 .","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 11 14","keyReferences":["1Chr 11 14","1Chr 16 35","1Sam 4 8","1Sam 7 3","1Sam 7 14","1Sam 10 18","1Sam 12 10","1Sam 12 11"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":213,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 11 14","book":"1Chr","chapter":11,"verse":14,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יַּצִּיל֔וּ/הָ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vhw3mp/Sp3fs"},{"reference":"1Chr 16 35","book":"1Chr","chapter":16,"verse":35,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/הַצִּילֵ֖/נוּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vhv2ms/Sp1cp"},{"reference":"1Sam 4 8","book":"1Sam","chapter":4,"verse":8,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"יַצִּילֵ֔/נוּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVhi3ms/Sp1cp"},{"reference":"1Sam 7 3","book":"1Sam","chapter":7,"verse":3,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/יַצֵּ֥ל","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vhi3ms"},{"reference":"1Sam 7 14","book":"1Sam","chapter":7,"verse":14,"englishText"